[BUREAU OF ENGINEERING]
BPW-2026-0602
CD 2, 6, 7
TEMPORARY FULL STREET CLOSURES AND ESTABLISHMENT OF ADMINISTRATIVE PROCESSING – EAST SAN FERNANDO VALLEY LIGHT RAIL TRANSIT PROJECT
Recommending the Board:
FIND that the Board has reviewed and considered the environmental documentation for the East San Fernando Valley Transit Corridor temporary full street closure program and the Bureau of Engineering (BOE) Environmental Management Division (EMD) responsible-agency review memorandum;
FIND, based on the environmental documentation and responsible-agency review included in the record, that the temporary full street closure program does not require a subsequent Environmental Impact Report or negative declaration under the California Environmental Quality Act Guidelines Section 15162 and will remain subject to the applicable Mitigation Monitoring and Reporting Program;
APPROVE, subject to the conditions identified in this report, the Project-wide program of temporary full street closures at the 65 cross streets identified in the project closure schedule, recognizing that the dates, durations, work hours, staging, and sequencing shown are planning estimates that will be refined as construction progresses;
SPECIFY that the Los Angeles County Metropolitan Transportation Authority (Metro) submit any temporary full street closure request to the City Engineer, or designee, for administrative review and permitting pursuant to the City Engineer's authority under the Los Angeles Municipal Code, the applicable Worksite Traffic Control Plan and detour-plan process, and the criteria and conditions set forth in this report;
SPECIFY that individual closures at the locations identified in Transmittal No. 3 will not require a separate Board Report, provided the proposed closure remains within the Project-wide approval granted by this report, is supported by the applicable environmental review, and satisfies the City Engineer's administrative review requirements;
NOTE that under existing permitting authority, the City Engineer may impose additional conditions; modify or limit a proposed closure; require additional technical analysis, interagency coordination, or outreach; or decline to issue the applicable permit when necessary to protect public safety, mobility, access, environmental compliance, or the public interest;
SPECIFY that the Metro Transit Division (MTD) and EMD of the BOE, the Board, and other relevant City of Los Angeles departments are custodians of the documents and other materials that constitute the record of proceedings upon which the Board's decision is based; and
DIRECT the BOE’s MTD, in coordination with the Metro, to include as part of the existing quarterly Metro project briefings to the Board, a citywide summary of active and upcoming temporary full street closures associated with the Metro projects, including the project, closure location, anticipated dates, duration, and status.
(W.O.: E1908502)
